              "content": "H4d — desktop pair of the Owner's selection: LIGHT = board 09 Option G2 · DARK = ‘Phones · DARK (header kept)’",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 24,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "xSRRq",
              "name": "Desc",
              "fill": "#5E5B55",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1440,
              "content": "Owner 2026-09-28: ‘build it from the 2 I selected — the sidebar uses the same colour as the mobile header, and the content too.’ LIGHT: Sidebar/shell #E4E4E7 (surface.muted, = G2 header), switcher = desktop Sidebar switcher (#FFFFFF, border #E4E4E7, text #18181B, chevrons #52525B), nav text/icons #52525B, active nav = white pill + #18181B label + lime-800 icon (#3F6212 — lime on white fails contrast), dividers #D4D4D8; content = G2 content (panel #F4F4F5, hero/cards/table #FFFFFF). DARK: Sidebar #18181B, raised #27272A, border #3F3F46, text #FFFFFF / #A1A1AA, lime icon (= mobile dark header); content = dark tokens (#09090B panel, #18181B cards, #27272A borders, #FAFAFA / #D4D4D8 / #A1A1AA text). FIX (Owner: ‘in dark the header merges with the sidebar — check the light scale’): light layers are sidebar 200 / panel 100 / cards 0 = surface.muted / surface.canvas / surface.panel. Both sidebars are now bound to those EXISTING tokens (sidebar surface.muted, switcher & active nav surface.panel + border.default, dividers border.input, text text.primary / text.secondary, active icon accent.soft-fg, chevron text.muted), so dark resolves to sidebar #27272A / panel #09090B / cards #18181B — no merge, no new tokens. Panel border (Owner: ‘add a border to the content panel, light & dark, find the right scale’): border.input (#D4D4D8 light / #3F3F46 dark) — one step off the shell (surface.muted #E4E4E7 / #27272A) in both modes; border.default would equal the shell and vanish. Implies retargeting component.panel.app.border → border.input.",
