              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• A — Grouped cards: closest to F-03/F-04, lowest build risk, every piece already in the library. Long lists get tall; price is secondary.",
              "fontFamily": "$k:font/family/base",
              "fontSize": "$k:font/size/body",
              "fontWeight": "$k:font/weight/regular"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "LqFs2",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$k:color/semantic/text/secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• B — Table + summary: best for many services and scanning prices; inline values speed edits. Summary panel adds a second place to keep in sync; phones need a different layout.",
              "fontFamily": "$k:font/family/base",
              "fontSize": "$k:font/size/body",
              "fontWeight": "$k:font/weight/regular"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "C0qUVL",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$k:color/semantic/text/secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• C — Master–detail: fastest switching between services, one screen. Most complex to build and test; needs a selected-row state the library doesn't have yet (used surface.muted fill); phones fall back to A.",
              "fontFamily": "$k:font/family/base",
              "fontSize": "$k:font/size/body",
              "fontWeight": "$k:font/weight/regular"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vDIO3",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$k:color/semantic/text/secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• D — Package cards: reads like a client price list, friendly for photographers. Least dense; booking preview makes fields concrete but editing happens elsewhere (dialog).",
              "fontFamily": "$k:font/family/base",
              "fontSize": "$k:font/size/body",
              "fontWeight": "$k:font/weight/regular"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "B1sg9j",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$k:color/semantic/text/secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• Mixing is possible, e.g. A list + B summary panel, or B table for Item paket (C2) under any option.",
              "fontFamily": "$k:font/family/base",
              "fontSize": "$k:font/size/body",
              "fontWeight": "$k:font/weight/regular"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "SJqSV",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$k:color/semantic/text/secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• Tokens: no new variables (606 before and after); all colours, type and spacing from k: semantic/component tokens. Local pieces: price text, fact rows, checklist rows, overline group labels.",
              "fontFamily": "$k:font/family/base",
              "fontSize": "$k:font/size/body",
              "fontWeight": "$k:font/weight/regular"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
